  "floating_noise_note": "Sweep rows rebuild the prime channel from floating atom vectors (relative calibration error at most 2.5e-13 against the Arb channel). The full-cell row (P = Q) therefore differs from the native slice by that reconstruction error: its minima are -3e-14 to -4e-13 at L = 4, 5 and -1.2e-12 (7 values below -1e-12) at L = 6, while the direct floating spectrum of the native slice bottoms out at -4e-15 to -8e-15. None of these is a negativity claim; no positive bottom is claimed at L = 5 or 6 (Increment 2B), and the certified L = 6 statement is the 1/4 checkpoint. Truncated rows are floating except the certified truncations at L = 4, 5.",
  "findings": {
    "channel_cancellation_on_V": "On the near-null subspace V (threshold 1e-2; dimension 51/50, 142/141, 346/345 at L = 4, 5, 6) -arch has extremes of order -2 and +5 and -prime mirrors them; the joint form is in [-5e-15, 7.5e-3]. Each channel alone is indefinite with O(1) eigenvalues on V (EXPERIMENTAL).",
    "arch_alone": "The slice form -arch alone is not positive: certified exact negative witnesses at L = 4, 5 (values -1.35, -0.94, -1.72, -1.19); floating minima -2.08 and -1.42 at L = 6.",
    "prime_truncation": "Positivity appears only at the full prime cell. Dropping only the largest prime power gives certified negative values at L = 4 (q = 53: -1.06e-5 even, -2.7e-3 odd) and L = 5 (q = 139: -0.216, -0.271); floating -5.8e-8 and -1.3e-5 at L = 6 (q = 401). These truncated forms are not native objects.",
    "bottom_vector_budget": "At the bottom slice vector -arch is an O(1) positive budget (2.0-3.0) consumed by the prime atoms with little internal cancellation (sum |atom| / |sum| = 1.04-1.29); the partial sums reach zero only at the end of the cell.",
    "derived_family_comparison": "S_IR - S_tail = C Mid C^T with Mid > 0 certified at L = 4, 5 for degrees 8 and 64 (CERTIFIED_PSD_VIA_FACTORIZATION)."
  }
